											<article id="post-1080" class="et_pb_post post-1080 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-fan-fiction">
											<div class="et_post_meta_wrapper">
							<h1 class="entry-title">Here is 10 chapters from Batman_9635</h1>

						<p class="post-meta"> by <span class="author vcard"><a href="https://markcheverton.com/author/adm1n/" title="Posts by Mark Cheverton" rel="author">Mark Cheverton</a></span> | <span class="published">Oct 24, 2015</span> | <a href="https://markcheverton.com/category/fan-fiction/" rel="category tag">Fan Fiction</a> | <span class="comments-number"><a href="https://markcheverton.com/here-is-10-chapters-from-batman_9635/#respond">0 comments</a></span></p>
												</div>
				
					<div class="entry-content">
					<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Quest for Defeating Herobrine</p>
<p>Book #1</p>
<p>Message from the author:</p>
<p>What is Minecraft? Minecraft is a sandbox game (endless game) where you are in a world of blocks. There are two modes: Creative mode and Survival mode. In Creative mode, you have infinite blocks and gives you the ability to build whatever you want, but in Survival mode (which is the real game) is when you have a health and hunger bar, and you need to mine resources, like gold, iron, diamond, and more. You need to build a shelter to survive the night.</p>
<p>At night, monsters arrive. Such as: zombies, spiders, skeletons, endermans, and slimes. Though, if you don’t like monsters to show up, then you can turn your world to “Peaceful” mode.</p>
<p>My minecraft name is Batman_9635, and my minecraft friend, TBC44. I have started writing this book when I was 12 years old, in July 7th 2015, 2:40 p.m. All my life, I have been heard of the game “Minecraft”, and has been told that it was really addicting. I looked up minecraft.net, and I saw the game video of what it will be. I saw the video, and it was awesome.</p>
<p>So I went over other minecraft video tutorials, on how to survive, and so on. It became very interesting, to the point that I kept asking my parents to buy the game for me.</p>
<p>3 years later, when I became 11 years old, my parents FINALLY bought me minecraft, and I enjoyed it so much. It never gets boring for me. So if you don’t have minecraft, I recommend YOU to buy it.</p>
<p>By the way, I also have a YouTube channel. Here is the link:https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBELIFCoWdk5olt44I97bZQ</p>
<p>Link to Twitter account:</p>
<p>Both my YouTube and Twitter name is Batman_9635</p>
<p>Don’t forget to subscribe to me on YouTube, and to follow me on Twitter!</p>
<p>Special thanks to Mark Cheverton (author of Gameknight999 books) for helping me out with this book.</p>
<p>1</p>
<p>Planning to Invade</p>
<p>He was walking on the moon, with a look of hatred on his face. As soon as his face showed, all the zombies bowed down to him. “My fellow zombies”, He said in a very low and clear voice, making the other zombies shiver. “I am your king, Mazus-Everbleed. We are going to invade the users within minecraft on this server”. He brought out a big globe, as shiny as silver. That globe then showed the only two users on this server, that they are going to attack.</p>
<p>They are: Batman_9635 and TBC44. “But first, we need to build ships for each one of us, so we can travel to the very grounds of minecaft and take revenge on them. They have killed many of our ancestors that used to live on the grounds” Mazus, the zombie king said.</p>
<p>“But we were the first ones to attack them, that’s why they were killing our ancestors” said another zombie in the very back. Mazus, being outraged, threw a diamond axe at the zombie in the head, bringing down all his HP (health points) and three glowing balls of XP (experience points).</p>
<p>This forced all the other zombies to take a few steps back. “TODAY, WE WILL BUILD SHIPS FOR EVERY ZOMBIE, AND TAKE REVENGE ON THOSE TWO PATHETIC USERS AFTER WE FINISH!” The zombies cheered, and then started working. “Master” said the zombie commander, “Where do we get all those supplies?”</p>
<p>“We will take pieces of the moon and put them together, and then we will add a superchip to make it work.” “Yes, your majesty.” Said the zombie commander.</p>
<p>All the zombies started to dig for resources, mostly iron. Then, the zombie king made a loud evil laugh, making all the zombies wobble, and even make the moon shake too.</p>
<p>2</p>
<p>Surviving the Night</p>
<p>Batman_9635 and TBC44 were walking on the hills, a beautiful day to sit down and talk. “So… what would you like to do?” said TBC, waiting desperately for an answer. “Well, maybe we could play hide and&#8230;.wait a sec!” said Batman. “What?” “We need to build a shelter, quick.” So they ran up to a tree, breaking and collecting the Oak logs and turning it into Oak planks. Then, they made a crafting table.</p>
<p>“Quick, craft a wooden pickaxe!” said Batman, worrying when night time will arrive. “Ok” was TBC’s answer. So they were mining stone, lots of it, then turned into cobblestone after it had been mined.</p>
<p>In about fifteen minutes, they made their whole house out of cobblestone. The size of the house was 20&#215;20. Then, they crafted two doors at the front of their house. “Quick, let’s find some iron, so we can make iron sword, pickaxe, axe, shovel, hoe, and full iron armor.</p>
<p>“Let’s go look for iron in a cave, it’s easier instead of creating a mine.” They found a cave, put torches everywhere, and found lots of iron. “Hey, come over here, there are more than fifty blocks of iron in this section!” said TBC. “Okay, sure, I’m coming!” replied Batman.</p>
<p>They kept mining and mining iron, until their inventory got full. “We both have 64&#215;27 Iron, so….we mined 1,728 iron each, so x2 will be 3,456 iron! Wow!” TBC 44 said. “Now, let’s go back home.” Said Batman_9635.</p>
<p>Right when they came out of the cave, it was already nighttime. “Quick, to the house!” TBC said.</p>
<p>They made it to their house before the monsters could even reach them. “Quick, let’s make a furnace!” Batman said. They made multiple furnaces, so they won’t have to wait for the Iron ores to smelt to Iron ingots. In about five minutes, all the iron was smelted into ingots.</p>
<p>Then, they started crafting iron tools, weapons, and armor. By the time they finished, the ground zombies started to bang on the doors, almost breaking them, with other monsters waiting for them behind the zombies. The zombies broke in, and also the other monsters flooded their house.</p>
<p>“No…..” replied both Batman and TBC. The only thing they could do was slash through the monsters, and out of their house, and that’s what they did. “My health is dropping, I have half-a-heart.” said TBC. “Me too.” Said Batman.</p>
<p>They ate cooked pork chops and steak, causing their hunger bar to get full and making their health bar slowly regenerate. They kept running, and saw monsters coming from all directions at them. They killed many, but there were still more of them coming.</p>
<p>At last, a wolf came with a whole bunch of other wolfs behind him, helping them to attack the monsters. They kept attacking and attacking, but there were still more.</p>
<p>Finally, the sun rised, and all the monsters were on fire, except for Slimes, Endermans, and Creepers. They ran back to the caves and shadows – hiding from the sun.</p>
<p>“We did it!” said TBC. “Thanks to the wolves!” said Batman. TBC crouched down and took a look at the wolf that was standing at the front of the pack. “He must be the leader.” said TBC. He looked on the wolf’s name tag that was chained to the leash around his neck in a bone shape.</p>
<p>He looked at it carefully. “Zachariah is the name of the leader of the pack.” TBC said after a while. “Cool.” added Batman.</p>
<p>“I think we should use Zachariah as our pet.” TBC answered. “He can make good use of helping us attack the monsters of the night.” Said TBC.</p>
<p>3</p>
<p>Battle With</p>
<p>The King of the Enderman</p>
<p>The king of the enderman was sitting on a throne made of diamonds. As others awaited for his orders, Zeek-Lore looked on The Sphere of Pain, and saw Batman_9635 and TBC44 running about the land. They were killing some animals for food, but at the same time, they were looking for something.</p>
<p>“It’s them, again.” Said Zeek-Lore, the king of the enderman. He turned the globe around and looked at the moon, and saw moon-zombies planning to invade. He zoomed in closer, and saw that they were digging up resources, mostly iron, and were building something.</p>
<p>“Baradikuss,” said Zeek “GO SPY ON THE MOON ZOMBIES AND STEAL SOME RESOURCES THEN COME BACK!” Baradikuss, nodded his head in a shiver, then teleported to the moon.</p>
<p>At the moon, Baradikuss saw millions of zombies digging for resources and are also building. He teleported to other zombies, quickly picking up resources, then when his hand was full, he was about to teleport back, but Mazus-Everbleed saw him, he told him to stop, and drop those resources.</p>
<p>Without Baradikuss even responding, he teleported back to Zeek-Lore’s castle. The enderman, being filled with rage, screamed very loud, and killed about 10 zombies in the front row, filled with anger.</p>
<p>Back at the castle, Baradikuss dropped all the reources in front of his king. “Here you go, sir.” Said Baradikuss, bowing down really low.</p>
<p>“IS THIS HOW YOU GIVE THINGS TO YOUR KING?!?!” said the king of the enderman. “Sorry, sir.” Replied Baradikuss. Zeek threw his globe at Baradikuss’s head, but he teleported.</p>
<p>Zeek-Lore closed his eyes, and extending out his arms. With his mind, he imaging Baradikuss not having the ability to teleport, and to make him still. He opened his eyes, and it worked.</p>
<p>Baradikuss, about to cry, was being poured on with water. The enderman was having smoke come out of his body. He was flashing red again and again, until his health dropped to nothing, and disappeared with 3 glowing balls of XP.</p>
<p>“IF ANY ONE OF YOU DARE TO CHALLENGE ME, THEN YOU WILL END UP IN THE SAME FATE AS HIM.” Zeek said, filled with anger.</p>
<p>“WE WILL TAKE OUR REVENGE ON THOSE TWO USERS, BECAUSE THEY DON’T HAVE THE RIGHT TO TAKE OUR LAND” and he said, “ALL OF YOU, TELEPORT TO BATMAN_9635 AND TBC44 AND BRING THEM TO ME RIGHT NOW!!!</p>
<p>All the enderman in Zeek-Lore’s castle teleported away, and in a matter of ten seconds, teleported back with Batman_9635 and TBC 44. “What?” Batman said. “We were just walking in the jungle, and without seeing anything teleported here?!?!” He continued. The king of the enderman laughed.</p>
<p>“You fools fell into my trap.” He said, “And you two are going to die for taking our land.” “YOUR LAND?!” TBC said with frustration. “THIS IS OUR LAND, AND YOU DON’T HAVE THE RIGHT TO TAKE IT FROM US!” “Shh….you will just make him angrier” Batman whispered in TBC’s ear.</p>
<p>Zeek, starting to get angry, closed his eyes and imagined that they were burning on fire, and they were. “How did this happen” TBC said. “I don’t know. We can’t let them see us burn to ashes. Get out your bucket of water.” Batman replied. They splashed a bucket of water on them, then after the fire on them faded away, they scooped up the water.</p>
<p>The same process was happening over and over again, until Zeek-Lore became angry. He brought out his fist, and smashed their faces hard, throwing both of them to the wall, and it literally got a crack on it then fell to the floor, the wall now shattered into thousands of pieces.</p>
<p>They flashed red, their HP about to drop. “We have to do something about this” said Batman. “We have only one choice – to attack.” “ARE YOU CRAZY?!?!” said TBC “First of all, there are thousands of enderman, and second, you hit one, they teleport next to you and kill you.” TBC continued, shaking with fear.</p>
<p>Batman, seeing him shake, told him; “STAND TALL AND BE BRAVE! There is only one choice, this is how we should react! Show them that we are ‘The Big Boys’ and that they are nothing compared to us!” “Ok then, let’s do this.” TBC replied.</p>
<p>They knew that water can kill enderman, and they had a whole bunch of buckets of water in their inventory. “Hey, check this out!” Batman said to everyone. The endermans looked at him, confused. “I have a gift of honour for all of you….AND IT’S A GIFT OF WATER!”</p>
<p>The two users dumped water all throughout the castle, literally flooding it. All the enderman couldn’t teleport away from that flood, and slowly, one by one, they all died, except for the king of the enderman, who heard their plan, but teleported outside. “WE DID IT!” TBC said with excitement.</p>
<p>They ran out of the castle and were going back home. They opened their doors, and saw Zeek-Lore in their house. They were shocked, but already were ready for the battle with the king of the enderman.</p>
<p>Zeek teleported to their side, and giving them a whole bunch of punches. Batman and TBC tried to dump water on Zeek, but he was too fast, and teleported away. And then a whole bunch of wolfs came to attack, but they all died, except for Zachariah, which was Batman’s most trusted wolf by his side.</p>
<p>They knew that endermans wouldn’t teleport away when you are slashing at their legs, so that’s what they did. Their iron sword was giving him lots and lots of damage, until he disappeared with a blue sphere. Batman, being surprised, picked up the blue sphere and read it. It said: Piece #1/10.</p>
<p>4</p>
<p>The Search for the Scroll</p>
<p>TBC44 both had a looks of confusion on their faces. “What is ‘Piece #1/10’?” TBC said. “I don’t know. Maybe we need to find the other nine pieces, then put them together, and it will turn into something.” Batman replied. “It also says two letters, which is ‘TE’.” Batman continued. “When I hold it, it feels like it’s trying to bring me into a direction.” Batman said again. “So, let’s see where it’s bringing you to.” TBC answered. So they kept walking into the direction that the silver globe was bringing them to.</p>
<p>On their way, they found a village. “Hey Batman, wanna take a break here?” “Sure.” They walked to the village, and saw many villagers. “Hi!” the villager said, “I’m villager #21.” “Batman and TBC were shocked, not because of the name, but because he can talk.</p>
<p>“Umm…..Hi?” TBC said. This made the villager frown. “Come, I have much to show you.” Villager #21 said. Right when they walked into the village others were saying “Hi, I’m villager #52…..Hi, I’m villager #81…..Hi, I’m villager #67…..” and so on.</p>
<p>Villager #21 was showing Batman and TBC around the village “Do you actually think that we should live here?” TBC whispered. “Sure! This place is much more protective.”  Batman whispered back. And nighttime approached.</p>
<p>“…..Or not.” Batman said again. Monsters were everywhere, and all the villagers went to their homes, hoping they won’t die tonight. “Let’s go back to the direction that we were supposed to go.” Said TBC</p>
<p>“No, not yet. We need to protect this village tonight, then in the morning, we can put cobblestone walls all around the village, so monsters won’t come in.” Batman said. “Sure” TBC replied.</p>
<p>They ran at the monsters, slashing and slashing, monsters flashing red and red, monsters disappearing and disappearing. A creeper ran up tp them, preparing to explode, but they were too fast for that green creature. They slashed at him three times, then he disappeared with gunpowder on the floor and three glowing balls of XP.</p>
<p>Then they ran up to the zombie, slashing at him, then at another monster, then another and another, until that whole area was cleared. At that moment, the sun came up, and all the villagers cheered their names.</p>
<p>That gave Batman and TBC a good feeling inside. “If you want to stay protected for your whole life, then why not build a wall made of cobblestone?” Batman shouted to the villagers. They all looked at each other with confusion.</p>
<p>Batman and TBC then started building cobblestone walls around the village, followed by a roof. This took them five minutes, since they were rushing. Batman and TBC said bye to the villagers, then continued on their journey.</p>
<p>“I can feel it.” Batman said. “We are getting closer.” They kept walking, and a few minutes later there was a flash of light that knocked them off their feet. They looked, and saw a scroll on the very top of a really high mountain.</p>
<p>“I’m not going to go mountain climbing. Why not make a TNT cannon that shoots us really high in the sky, and for us to land on the scroll?” Batman said. “Sounds fine to me.” TBC answered. They got out their dispensers, redstone dust, redstone capacitors, TNT, and water.</p>
<p>Batman put twelve dispensers in one row, and one dispenser facing a different direction at the end, then another twelve dispensers in one row facing the other dispensers. Then, he put redstone dust and redstone capacitors in front of each dispenser. Then, he put TNT all around it, and after that, water.</p>
<p>“This should shoot us all the way in the sky without taking any damage, since there is water around it.” TBC said. “That’s right!” Batman replied. TBC pulled the lever, and the TNT started to blink. “Ready?” TBC said. “Yes” Batman replied again. Then five seconds later, the TNT exploded.</p>
<p>They went extremely high up in the sky, then fell right next to the scroll, with lots of damage. “Yes! It’s the scroll!” Batman said. TBC remained silent. Batman held up the scroll, and the whole area flashed bright white. “Hey, TBC, take a look at this!” “Hmm?” TBC answered. “Read it.” Batman said.</p>
<p>There are 10 pieces you need to build a structure, a structure that you can use to see throughout the galaxy. Each piece tells you a letter, except for the first piece, it tells you 2 letters. In order to get those pieces, you must kill the evil kings, in The Overworld, in The End, and in The Nether. Once you receive these pieces, you put them together, and it will turn into a telescope.</p>
<p>5</p>
<p>Escape From the</p>
<p>Castle of the Skeleton King</p>
<p>Selk got out his enchanted bow. It was enchanted to everything –Unbreaking III, Fire III, Bane of Anthropods V, and etc. His throne was made of nothing but bones. He stood up, and brought his hand up in the air to silence his fellow skeletons. “Brothers” he continued, “It has been a long time since we haven’t killed any users.” He said again, “Now there are two. It is now time to search for users and kill them. Bring them to me alive, then I will take their heads, and decorate my throne with them.”</p>
<p>The skeletons nodded, and ran to look for users. Meanwhile, Batman_9635 and TBC44 were searching for a king to kill, so they can get the second piece. But ahead of them, they could see skeletons everywhere, looking for something. “Let’s follow them to see where they’re going.” said TBC. “No, wait until they’re going back to where they are, then we will follow them.</p>
<p>“Fine, then I have to go by myself.” TBC said. Before Batman could even say anything, TBC put up his hand to silence his friend. This made Batman feel very insulted. So, TBC went to spy on the skeletons, waiting to see where they were going to go, but he failed.</p>
<p>The skeletons spotted TBC, and before he could even react, he was shot by one arrow, making him become stunned. This shocked Batman, and made him hide in the bushes, so he won’t be seen, while also going to watch what was going to happen.</p>
<p>The skeletons grabbed TBC, and brought him to the castle of the skeleton king. Batman was following them, hoping to save his friend if he could survive. They went into the castle, and the door was shut closed. It was too late for Batman could go in. All he could do was watch.</p>
<p>But wait…… He thought. I have to find a way inside to save my friend.And so, Batman was thinking of a plan of how to get inside first, then how to save his friend. He kept hearing voices from the castle; “You only have five minutes to live…… and then your head is mine.” Selk made a laugh that made others start to shiver.</p>
<p>Oh no….. He said to himself again, I have to react fast before my friend is dead….. Batman couldn’t break through the castle, because it was made out of bedrock and bones. Batman was starting to get angry, so he started running around the castle, and he accidentally stepped on a pressure plate, which opened by four blocks. And of course, he fell down.</p>
<p>He started screaming with anger, until he fell down into an underground swamp. Luckily, he landed into the pool, but if he landed on that ground, then he wouldn’t’ve survived. Batman looked straight ahead, and saw a redstone elevator. He went on it, and about two minutes later, he got to the top.</p>
<p>He was in the castle. But where in the castle am I? The castle is huge, and anytime the skeleton king will kill my friend! Batman said to himself. He got out his map, and saw that he was near. He ran straight ahead, but then ran back, because there were guards. Batman brought out his bow, and secretly shot the skeleton guards one by one, until they were all gone.</p>
<p>Batman ran straight ahead, but then was in shock. A skeleton already lifted up its diamond axe, about to slash TBC 44 in the neck. Just before that skeleton slashed at TBC, the skeleton has been shot in the head by Batman’s bow. He quickly ran and grabbed TBC’s hand, then ran away.</p>
<p>“STOP HIM!” the skeleton king shouted. And this time, he didn’t sit on his throne and wait for the skeletons to bring him back. He stood up, and ran after them. “This castle is a huge maze!” Batman shouted in a whisper in TBC’s ear. He could now move again.</p>
<p>“I thought I was going to die, but it was a miracle that you found your way to get into the castle, find me, then save me.” TBC whispered back. “Tell me which way the skeletons brought you inside.” Batman said.</p>
<p>“Turn left&#8230;now, right…right again…left&#8230;downstairs&#8230;fifth chamber…and then keep going straight. The redstone elevator must be there – It’s our only way out, since the doors are closed and locked.” They kept running faster and faster, and finally reached the redstone elevator, but unluckily, one of the skeletons pulled the lever, and they fell down all the way to the ground. “They’re dead.” Said one of the skeletons. “Let’s go back.” Said another.</p>
<p>After all that pain, Batman and TBC woke up, both of them exactly at half a heart. That was how much health they both had lost, starting from nine hearts. “Here, the exit is there.” TBC said. They walked to the exit, and when they came out of the castle, they ran for their lives back to their house, so they can wait for their health to regenerate, and for them to enchant their weapons to high levels, then they will continue on their journey.</p>
<p>6</p>
<p>The End</p>
<p>Batman_9635 and TBC 44 were enchanting their own weapons to a really high level. “You hear that?” TBC said while he was shaking.” “What? Why are you shaking? You are acting weird…you have never been like this before.” Batman answered. “I’m having visions…terrifying visions… like a black dragon with purple eyes staring at me, and a whole bunch of enderman on a floating island…” TBC said in a terrified voice.</p>
<p>“That must be The End. The End always gives people nightmares and terrifying visions when you think about it…” Batman continued, “In order for your fears to be gone, we have to fight the enderdragon.” “The ender what-what?” TBC said “EN – DER – DRA – GON!” Batman said, about to become frustrated.</p>
<p>“We have to kill it.” Batman said again. “But there are many problems – first of all, we need to find the end portal dungeon, second of all, we need to find the end portal within that dungeon, and third of all, we need to find out and plan how to kill the enderdragon.” Batman said. But first, we need to find diamonds.</p>
<p>They kept mining and mining for hours, and they found lots of diamonds, but still they kept mining until their inventory will get full. They kept mining, and mining, and mining, and mining, and mining, and now, they have 64&#215;27 diamonds, which was what they needed.</p>
<p>They went all the way back up, and into their house. They made lots of diamond swords, axes, shovels, pickaxes, hoes, and armor. Then they enchanted their tools and armor to a very high level.</p>
<p>Batman looked outside just to see if its day or night, and it was night. They were just about to sleep, but then they heard banging on their doors. “Quickly, to the escape tunnel! There are lots of mobs banging at our door, and they sound angry. Perhaps there are hundreds, and we can’t underestimate them!” Batman shouted. He opened up a trap door, which was in the top left corner of the house, and both of them went down the ladder, with TBC closing the trapdoor, so the mobs won’t see them escaping.</p>
<p>“Remember we planted TNTs around our house? Well, here is the lever. It’s the only way to get rid of those mobs.” Batman whispered “But our house…” “No ‘Ifs or buts!’” TBC pulled the lever, and in seconds, they heard boom. Batman and TBC climbed back up, and saw their house blown to oblivion, and the mobs gone.</p>
<p>They both didn’t have time to rebuild their house, but instead, decided to live in a village. Batman and TBC were going toward the direction of the village, since they knew that they were the ones who build the walls around that village.</p>
<p>When Batman and TBC arrived, they asked their village leader to live here. “Sure” the leader responded. So both of them went inside. The village was huge, and there was a well in the center. “Hey, let’s start building a redstone trap for the mobs!” TBC questioned. “Sure.”</p>
<p>They ran to the well, hopped in, and started digging downward to start building a redstone trap somewhere. But something strange happened. They fell down, and landed inside a dungeon.</p>
<p>Batman and TBC looked around “What is this place?” TBC asked “I know it…it looks familiar…” Batman continued, “Wait a sec…It’s a dungeon! The End portal is somewhere here. We need to just stick together, and run around the place to find the portal.” “Alright.”</p>
<p>At that moment, they heard a door creaking open, and they have been pulled in by a magnet. They went up a set of steps, and didn’t believe what they saw. It was The End portal. “The magnet that just pulled us in must’ve been the portal. Oh well, time to face our fears.” TBC said. They looked at each other, then jumped in, and both of them disappeared in a wave, like water being evaporated.</p>
<p>7</p>
<p>Battle with the Enderdragon</p>
<p>They both looked around, trying to find The Enderdragon. Both of them saw nothing but a whole bunch of enderman. “Don’t look at them in the eye! Even if you do by accident, they will teleport next to us and then, it will be our last second of life!” Batman whispered in TBC’s ear, but sounded in a little bit of a shout. “OK, ok…I know…fine…” TBC replied, sounding a little exhausted.</p>
<p>Batman looks up, and sees some kind of figure flying in the sky. He shoved his elbow into TBC, making him look up. He was shocked. “It’s him…the dragon in my nightmare…” TBC said, terrified.</p>
<p>Suddenly, a shiver ran down TBC’s spine, and it was a feeling of hatred and fear. Both of them ran straight forward, and saw lots of obsidian pillars stretching up all the way to the sky, and the ender crystal at the very top of each pillar. Those crystals regenerate The Enderdragon’s health.</p>
<p>“Quick, let’s destroy those crystals!” Batman said. They grabbed their bow, and started shooting at the crystals. They kept missing, because it was very high up. Finally TBC lost aim and accidentally hit the crystal next to it on another pillar. It caused a big explosion, and made The Enderdragon look straight directly into TBC’s eyes. At that moment, TBC fainted.</p>
<p>Batman quickly catched TBC before he fell backwards into the ground. The Enderdragon looked straight at the users, his anger starting to get over control, then charged right at them. “TBC!!!!” Batman said, trying not to get extremely angry – “Can’t you just stand up and run beside me instead of me dragging you everywhere!?!</p>
<p>“Uuuggghhh….” TBC struggled, still unconscious a little. “Hurry, the Enderdragon is charging at us!” Batman shouted.</p>
<p>“Huh?” TBC said, confused, when he just woke up from his unconsciousness.</p>
<p>“Quickly, follow me….”</p>
<p>TBC sprinted toward Batman, and saw him shoot up at more ender crystals, and so, TBC started doing the same thing. In a matter of minutes, all the crystals has exploded (That’s what happens when you hit a crystal). The Enderdragon tried looking for more ender crystals, but they weren’t any. It had no choice, but to charge.</p>
<p>“INCOMING!” TBC shouted, with a mixture of anger and fear in his voice. Batman remained silent, got out his sword, and slashed it at the dragon while it was charging, making it flash red. TBC got out his bow, then kept shooting arrows at it. More flashes of red, but The Enderdragon was still charging, heading straight for TBC.</p>
<p>He told me in my dream that my time will come…that’s why he is coming straight at me… My nightmare is coming. My time is over. TBC thought to himself. “PULL THE LEVER!” Batman shouted to TBC, but he just stood still, as in something or someone was controlling his mind, and remained silent.</p>
<p>Batman was getting frustrated, but at the same time, there was only one question in his mind that hasn’t been solved; what is wrong with TBC44? Batman quickly sprinted behind TBC and pulled the lever behind him. Just before The Enderdragon charged into TBC by a meter, the TNT exploded, throwing Batman, TBC, and The Enderdragon into the air.</p>
<p>Batman quickly dumped a bucket of water on where they both will land, so they won’t take any damage. It worked. “What is wrong with you?” Batman said aloud in TBC’s ear. “Who are you? What is this place? Get away from me!” TBC said. “Batman, being confused, ran away from TBC44 and started fighting The Enderdragon by himself</p>
<p>Something is going on here. First, he didn’t move, and looked like he was about to commit suicide. Next, he acted like he didn’t know this place; didn’t know me. The Enderdragon was about to charge again, looking weak. Batman shouted at The Enderdragon; “WHAT HAVE YOU DONE TO MY FRIEND?!” and then gave it a few strong and big slashes to The Enderdragon with his diamond sword, and something strange happened.</p>
<p>The Enderdragon died. Batman was expecting it to pop. But instead, The Enderdragon stopped moving, then slowly was going up high in the sky, the black particles slowly turning white, white lights flashing up in all directions, and then slowly faded away, with a shower of XP’s (yellow glowing balls) falling down upon him.</p>
<p>Batman suddenly started to feel stronger, and now has the thoughts of The Enderdragon in his mind. Now he knew what happened with TBC44. By The Enderdragon looking straight into TBC’s eyes, he completely erased his mind. Batman was thinking deeper into The Enderdragon’s thoughts for a cure… and he found it!</p>
<p>It was stupid, but however, he needed to do it – for the sake of his friend. He had to keep hitting him with his diamond sword until he has no hearts left, and just before he pops, Batman needed to quickly throw a splash potion of healing on TBC, and so, he did.</p>
<p>“What…what just happened? I was right there then I moved here?!” TBC said, unsure of what is going on. “Do you know who I am?” Batman questioned. “Of course I do! Why are you asking me this?” “Long story.”</p>
<p>“We need to collect that dragon egg” Batman said in a ‘bossy’ voice. He put a block of redstone on the left, below the dragon egg. Then, he put a sticky piston right on top of the redstone block, but facing the egg, and right away, it shoved the egg and Batman collected it. (You can’t just pick up a dragon egg in minecraft, because it will teleport somewhere else. You basically have to make a sticky piston move it – somehow).</p>
<p>Batman_9635 and TBC44 gave each other a high – five, then jumped into the portal back to the overworld</p>
<p>8</p>
<p>Into The Nether</p>
<p>TBC44 and Batman_9635 spawned somewhere in the overworld, but they still knew where they were, since they had a map with them. “We need to go back to the village. We aren’t that far from the village. Hooray!” Batman said with excitement. They kept running for about 2 minutes, and then they reached their destination. It’s them! They are back to save us when we get attacked tonight!” said villager #12 gladly. All the other villagers cheered. “Zachariah” Batman shouted his name. All of a sudden you see an enormous pack of wolfs coming at you, and in the front, Zachariah, Batman’s most trusted wolf.</p>
<p>“Guard the perimeter, and watch out for monsters. If you see any, don’t fight them, instead report it to us. I’m not gonna risk any of yourselves lives for this, like last time, when we were battling the king of the enderman. The whole pack died, except for Zachariah, but finally, thanks to him, he found a pack” Batman said seriously.</p>
<p>The wolves did as commanded, and went around the village wall and started guarding the perimeter. It became nighttime in a few minutes, and Batman was looking around him, looking out for monsters, while TBC was sleeping.</p>
<p>Batman quickly ran up to TBC, “Wake up! It’s nighttime!” Batman shouted to TBC in the ear. “You’re right, it is nighttime, but did you know that nighttime is also sleeping time?” TBC mocked. “Well, did you know that nighttime can also be monster time?” Batman mocked back.</p>
<p>“Okay, okay, fine, sorry” TBC44 said exhaustingly. TBC jumped off his bed, and ran with Batman outside the village, and helping him guard it. Suddenly, they heard hissing. “It’s a creeper…It’s about to explode!” TBC shouted. He quickly did a backflip, grabbed Batman’s hands in mid-air, then Batman threw TBC to the creeper, and he killed it in mid-air doing a kick, in a split second.</p>
<p>“Nice job back there, bud” Batman said, surprised of what TBC did. “I hear rumbling…and lots of moans…It’s the zombies!” Batman said, in a surprised voice “It sounds like 10…maybe 15…”Batman said. “SNAP OUT OF IT! THERE ARE ZOMBIES COMING!” TBC shouted very loud, making almost every villager wake up.</p>
<p>TBC quickly ran toward the zombies, but Batman stopped him “What are you doing?” TBC said. “I can handle this” Batman replied. Batman quickly stepped back, pulled out two diamond swords from his back on both hands, and charged for the zombies. He stabbed the lead zombie, spun, then threw it at the other zombies.</p>
<p>Batman then spun like an unstoppable tornado, slicing at zombies with both of his diamond swords. Then he jumped really high, tilted his body a little bit to the right with both diamond swords facing downward, then landed very fast with both diamond swords stabbed downward at two zombies, then stabbed the last zombie coming behind him, with both swords at the same time. Suddenly the Sun appeared, filling all of minecraft with warm light.</p>
<p>TBC looked at Batman, both eyes wide in shock. But that moment has been cut, since there was a villager running out of the jungle in front of Batman_9635 and TBC44. “They are coming!” said the villager. “Who is coming?” Batman and TBC said at the same time, then looked at each other. “The Nether creatures…They’re coming!” All of a sudden, there was an army of blazes, zombie-pigmen, magma cubes, withered skeletons, and ghasts.</p>
<p>“How can we fight this zombie horde?” TBC said. “Teamwork” Batman said, looking straight into TBC’s eyes with a smile. They both quickly jumped high into the air and landed on the upcoming monsters, slashing at them, and bringing their HP to zero. Batman threw TBC really high in the air, with lots of other monsters. Monsters were raining on TBC like a shower, but he kept hitting them in the face with his feet, nearly consuming their HP, then the monsters died when they landed, and Batman catching TBC.</p>
<p>Batman then spun like a whirlwind with both his diamond swords, slashing side-by-side any monster that gets near him. Soon, all the monsters died, with the blazes and ghasts the last ones to be standing. All of a sudden, there was a shower of fireballs coming upon them. But Batman ant TBC were very fast at dodging, and haven’t got hit by any fireball.</p>
<p>Batman quickly put both his swords on his back, and started throwing batarangs at the blazes, literally killing them with every throw. After all the blazes died, TBC threw his diamond sword at one ghast, killing it, and then it bounced on the other ghasts, killing them. The diamond sword came flying straight toward TBC, then caught it.</p>
<p>Suddenly, an enderman teleported right behind them. Batman and TBC looked back and was shocked at what they saw. “You…we killed you…How are you still alive?” Batman said. The king of the enderman laughed. “You fool. You didn’t notice that I can respawn?!” Then he laughed again. “Your times are about to come to an end.” The enderman said “And how will that happen?” TBC questioned.</p>
<p>The enderman laughed again, but this time, even louder. He quickly grabbed Batman_9635 and TBC44 then teleported into The Nether. “Have fun guys!” He laughed very hard, but before Batman and TBC could catch him, he teleported back to the overworld. “We need to make a plan to get out of The Nether, and go back to the overworld” said TBC, and so, he explained the plan.</p>
<p>9</p>
<p>Escaping The Nether</p>
<p>Both Batman_9635 and TBC44 were walking for about 2 hours without any talk or trouble. All of a sudden, a nether fortress appeared from sight. “That must be the way out of this place!” TBC said in an excitement. “No, the nether fortress is a highly dangerous place were the worst of the worst kind of monst-” Batman replied, but was suddenly cut off when TBC was running into the Nether fortress.</p>
<p>He ran after TBC for a long while saying “Hey, wait up!” TBC ran into a blaze, but before it could even react, Batman shot out his grapnel gun at it, then pulled the blaze fast, and kicked it. The blaze threw a fireball at Batman, but he was too fast for the blaze.</p>
<p>Batman dodged the incoming fireball, and threw a batarang at the blaze. “Is this all you got?” the blaze replied in his mechanical voice. “No” Batman replied, and pressed a button on his hand. The batarang exploded, and the blaze was gone.</p>
<p>Batman_9635 and TBC44 didn’t know where to go, so they decided to wander around the dangerous place until they find a way out. All of a sudden, a blaze appeared right in front of them. It wasn’t like any blaze they have seen before – It was enormous.</p>
<p>“WELCOME TO YOUR DOOM…THE PROPHECY STATES THAT TWO USERS WOULD SAVE ALL OF MINECRAFT…WELL I AM HERE TO STOP THAT.”</p>
<p>He replied in his mechanical voice. “This must be the blaze king” TBC replied. “You’re right, he is the blaze king” Batman said, shocked. The blaze king roared loudly, making many pieces of the Nether fortress fall into the lava.</p>
<p>Batman and TBC were about to fall in the lava, and at the same time, the blaze king threw a gigantic fireball at them. Batman quickly brought out his grapnel gun, and shot back at the Nether fortress, and grabbed TBC. The grapnel gun pulled themselves back to the Nether fortress fast.</p>
<p>The blaze king roared even louder. “AAAAA!!! MY EARS!!!” TBC shouted. Luckily, nothing happened to Batman. He was thinking about something else, pretending there was no such thing. “Just don’t think about the sound” Batman replied.</p>
<p>“Stay here, I can handle this.” Batman said to TBC. He took out his grapnel gun, shot is at the blaze king, and he has been pulled to his target fast. Batman was now on the blaze king’s head. Fire was all over the blaze’s head, but nothing happened to Batman, since his suit was fireproof.</p>
<p>He took out both his tasers on each hand, placed it on the head of the blaze king, used his grapnel gun, shot it right in front of TBC’s legs, and was pulled there in a matter of seconds. Batman then took out a joystick from his belt, pressed the button, and then the tasers were activated.</p>
<p>Bolts of electricity shot out through every part of the blaze, making it collapse after it has been struck with more than a million volts, and down he went. Batman jumped down and started cape gliding towards his fallen enemy, while TBC jumped on Batman’s back, and started to glide with him.</p>
<p>They landed on the blaze king smoothly. “HOW DO WE GET OUT OF HERE?!” Batman shouted at the top of his lungs into the blaze king’s ear. “LOOKS LIKE…*cough* *cough* THE PROPHECY *cough* WAS TRUE.” The blaze king said off topically. “I SAID HOW?!?!” Batman said louder, stabbing the blaze king with his diamond sword.</p>
<p>“YOU WILL…*cough* *cough* HAVE TO…*cough* KILL ME…*cough* *cough*” the blaze king replied. “…BUT YOU WONT MAKE IT *cough* YOU WILL NEVER GET PAST *cough* THE MAKER *cough* *cough* *cough* HE…” and suddenly his yellow eyes faded to black, along with his body, then was separated into millions of pieces. The blaze king is now dead.</p>
<p>“Now that was sad. You were very harsh on him.” TBC said, sadly. “Don’t be sad. He was trying to kill us.” Batman replied. “That’s true, but it’s not his fault. Didn’t you hear him? It was the Maker. He was forced to obey the Maker’s command, therefore he was created by him.” TBC answered</p>
<p>“…the Maker…” Batman whispered to himself. Suddenly, the Nether started to shake. A flash of white formed as he appeared. He had dark blue pants with a turquoise shirt, and was hovering in the air. But his eyes…something was strange. His eyes glowed bright white.</p>
<p>“WHAT HAVE YOU DONE TO MY CHILDA?!” He shouted. “That must’ve been the Maker” TBC whispered. The strange figure shot out a glow of fireball at Batman and TBC, knocking them off cold. All of a sudden they swapped dimensions, and were thrown into the overworld.</p>
<p>The strange figure teleported back to the overworld, then gave Batman and TBC a flying uppercut with a trail of fire. “I WILL RETURN. AND THIS TIME, I WILL CRUSH BOTH OF YOU WITH MY BARE HANDS.” And then he disappeared, his eyes the last to fade away. Batman and TBC looked at each other in shock at what just happened.</p>
<p>10</p>
<p>Herobrine Discovered</p>
<p>Batman_9635 and TBC 44 were running for their lives, hoping to find the village they found last time.</p>
<p>Hope you enjoyed what I&#8217;ve wrote so far, Mark! And if you could, I would kindly ask if you could show this to Gameknight999 and Monet113. Enjoy!</p>
